# Each contract check of tools/subject.bzl and tools/defs.bzl, fed a broken
# contract (see :contract_problems in BUILD.bazel): the case, a tab, and words
# its message must hold -- or OK, where nothing may be wrong. Read by
# //tools/tests:macro_fixtures_test.
audit-case-gate-folder	OK
audit-case-gate-no-folder	ex00_program_allocfail: the gate runs $(location :ex00_bin) on "42", from the test's own folder, against $(location tests/ex00/a.txt), and no output test of this package runs the program that way
audit-case-gate-stdin	ex00_beside_valgrind: the gate runs $(location :ex00_bin) on "42", from the test's own folder, against $(location tests/ex00/a.txt), and no output test of this package runs the program that way
audit-clues-keyed	OK
audit-clues-keyed-no-case	ex00_sweep: it hands ex00's keyed clues.tsv to its runner without --case
audit-clues-per-case	tests/ex00/clues_args.tsv: ex00 keys its hints to its cases (--case, as ex00_a_output does)
audit-clues-read	OK
audit-clues-unread	tests/ex00/clues_other.tsv: no test of this package hands it to a runner
audit-argv-guarded	OK
audit-argv-unguarded	ex00_argv_diff_asan: it replays an argument corpus under ASan on $(location :ex00_bin_asan), and ex00 has a guarded build, :ex00_argvguard_bin_asan
audit-corpus-asan-on-plain	ex00_sweep_diff_asan: it replays its corpus with --sanitized on a program that is not an ASan build
audit-corpus-covers	OK
audit-corpus-covers-nothing	ex00_sweep_diff_asan: its corpus_memory() covers ex00_swept, which is no plain replay of a corpus in this package
audit-corpus-covers-twinned	ex00_sweep_diff_asan: its corpus_memory() covers ex00_sweep, whose own corpus has a twin already (ex00_sweep_diff_asan)
audit-corpus-each-twinned	OK
audit-corpus-judging-options	OK
audit-corpus-no-asan	ex00_sweep: it replays a generated corpus (its runner's default corpus) through //tools:rush01_check.sh on the plain build, and no test replays that corpus under ASan/UBSan
audit-corpus-memory-rule-missing	ex00_sweep_valgrind: it replays a corpus under memcheck quoting no rule, and ex00_run_valgrind quotes the subject's own sentence
audit-corpus-memory-rule-quoted	OK
audit-corpus-no-malloc	OK
audit-corpus-no-memcheck	ex00_sweep: its subject allows malloc, and no test replays its corpus (its runner's default corpus) under memcheck
audit-corpus-no-valgrind	ex00_bsq_diff: its subject allows malloc, and no test replays its corpus (--fn maps) under memcheck
audit-corpus-ok	OK
audit-corpus-two-transports	ex00_bsq_stdin: it replays a generated corpus (--fn maps --mode stdin) through //tools:rush01_check.sh on the plain build, and no test replays that corpus under ASan/UBSan
audit-below-its-suffix	ex00_exit: it sits at basic, below its _exit layer's robust.
audit-empty-manual-tag	ex00_output: the no_manual_test_in_this_module tag is the empty :manual suite's, and no test may carry it.
audit-exercise-without-test	ex01: the exercise has no test, so its //c-piscine/c-piscine-toy:ex01 runs nothing
audit-fixture-prototype-declared	OK
audit-fixture-prototype-missing	ex00_bin: a harness over a student's function names ex00_prototype as the test of its signature, and this package declares no such test
audit-gate-case-run	OK
audit-gate-no-argument	ex00_sweep, ex00_sweep_diff_asan: the gate runs $(location :ex00_bin) with no argument against $(location tests/ex00/example.txt), and no output test of this package runs the program that way
audit-gate-stdin-case	ex00_sweep, ex00_sweep_diff_asan: the gate runs $(location :ex00_bin) with no argument
audit-harness-untagged	ex00_diffbin: it links a harness over a student's files and carries no prototype_test= tag
audit-ladder	ex00_output: its lvl_* tags (lvl_basic) are not a level and every level above it
audit-layout-read	OK
audit-layout-tag-read	OK
audit-layout-tag-unread	tests/layout/tag/toy.h: no test of this package reads it
audit-layout-twin-basic	ex00_layout_prototype: it sits at basic, below its _layout_prototype layer's strict
audit-layout-twin-strict	OK
audit-layout-unread	tests/layout/toy.h: no test of this package reads it (no exNN_prototype or exNN_layout_prototype passes it with --layout or --layout-tag)
audit-manual-in-fixtures	OK
audit-manual-listed	OK
audit-manual-unlisted	ex00_output: it is manual, so no suite and no /... pattern runs it, and tools/defs.bzl's _MANUAL does not list it
audit-no-exercise-tag	ex00_diff: it has no ex00 tag, so //c-piscine/c-piscine-toy:ex00 does not run it
audit-no-layer	ex00_diff: it carries 0 layer tags (none)
audit-not-an-exercise	check: a project's test is named exNN_<what>, after its exercise
audit-ok	OK
audit-raise-listed	OK
